<code>assert this.containsEdge(e) == added;</code>

However, based on the comment "@@@ The graph contains the edge returned by the method.", it seems more appropriate to directly assert that the graph contains the edge `e` after the method execution:

<code>assert this.containsEdge(e);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.containsEdge(e) == added;</code>

However, based on the comment, it seems more appropriate to assert that the graph contains the edge that was just added. Therefore, the correct assert statement would be:

<code>assert added => this.containsEdge(e);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.containsEdge(e) == \result;</code>
--------------------
